<title>UK: UK clears Prudential, ScotAm merger.</title>
<headline>UK clears Prudential, ScotAm merger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK government on Thursday cleared the proposed takeover of mutually-owned insurance group Scottish Amicable by Prudential Corp Plc.</p>
<p>Trade and Industry Secretary Margaret Beckett said in a statement she had decided not to refer the merger to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission, in accordance with the recommendation of the Director General of Fair Trading.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
